# A PDF's cross-reference table stores ABSOLUTE BYTE OFFSETS. If Git rewrites its line endings on
# checkout (autocrlf is on for this repo), every offset after the first newline is wrong and the file
# is silently corrupt — it may still open in a viewer while failing in a parser, which is the worst
# kind of broken. Mark the binary formats so Git copies them byte-for-byte.
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico  binary
*.rfa  binary
*.rvt  binary
*.ifc  binary

# DXF is plain text, but the AutoCAD family expects CRLF. Pin it so the sample file is byte-identical
# on every machine that clones this repo.
*.dxf  text eol=crlf
